{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/270560-a-houserule-ghosts-physical-bodies","id":270560,"title":"A houserule - ghosts physical bodies...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-01T20:53:09-07:00","id":270560,"title":"A houserule - ghosts physical bodies...","content":"Hey guys, I'm toying with the idea of a house rule that makes fighting ghosts physically (e.g. going to twilight and just punching them in the face) a little harder. Basically, I'm giving them access to dread powers. My intention is to give Ghosts a home field advantage when you fight them on their own turf by allowing them to re-imagine their bodies a little. I like the image of that sweat girl ghost turning into a horrible banshee when enraged, or the little boy sicking an eight foot tall teddy bear monster on you when you just wont leave him alone.<br /> <br /> I'm a little bit new to WoD so I was hoping someone could help me make sure my balance is ok and that I'm not missing anything silly...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(House rule) Twilight bodies:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the most part, Ghost\u2019s are ephemeral beings - they may appear to be real people but they\u2019re echoes and memories of who they used to physically be. They appear to be who they think they are and - sometimes purposely and other times inadvertently - take on grotesque forms. These forms depend largely on the ghost feeling some strong emotion and reflect the ghosts self image - a spurned lover might start to resemble a succubus of some sort while the suicidal linebacker might take the form of a statue. As a general rule, the older and more powerful a ghost is, the more extreme the transformation is and the more control they have over it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normally, these transformations only serve to unnerve or confuse mortals, but for a Sin-Eater who can potentially fight a ghost physically they provide a further complication. When physically fighting a ghost - such as in Twilight or the underworld - these forms can give the ghost an advantage. Those claws and teeth are dangerous weapons to others. Those wings can give them an escape route, and the stone body might provide defense.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mechanically, use Dread powers to represent these new physical capabilities - using their attribute dots as a rough guide for how many dots in dread powers they are capable of. Actually manifesting these abilities requires a successful power + finesse roll from the ghost if it wishes to use them, although the transformation becomes automatic if the ghost is enraged or otherwise driven by strong emotion.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":".  Formatting 10-01-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T22:08:23-07:00","id":270613,"title":"","content":"If you want to use this for a largely cosmetic change, or perhaps a non-Geist game, it could work.<br /> <br /> A competent group of Sin-Eaters could still devestate anything short of Sin-Eaters where anyone has the Stigmata Key or certain Ceremonies can still easily defeat a less than Rank 6 ghost. It's what they are built to do. Geist gives you an opportunity to have really cool stories interacting with ghosts, but if you want ghosts posting a major threat to more than starting characters (depending on build)...it's not what you want to run. So I guess the question is do you want to make them slightly more challenging or expecting a major challenge? Becuase if the latter, well-played Sin-Eaters have all sorts of ways to handle them.<br /> <br /> The main issue with Dread Powers is mostly just that it muddles with the Spirit rules. Insofar as you are okay with that have at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T00:55:20-07:00","id":270656,"title":"","content":"Considering that night stalkers talks about ghosts buying drain to become vampires, ghosts have dread powers isn't so much a house rule as the logical result of having dread powers in a geist game.<br /> <br /> If you want more versatile ghosts, you might want to take a look at gmc, ghosts can spend essence to enhance their stats and have influences, so even a rank one ghost could have defense 6 and an attack roll of 12 if they really need to spend the points for it, and at higher levels can get downright magey depending on what influences they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T01:49:28-07:00","id":270659,"title":"","content":"Ghosts having influences does help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T03:55:16-07:00","id":270706,"title":"","content":"That's very helpful actually. I missed the rules on influence. That said, so far influence rules seem very confusing. Are there any examples of spirits with influence and what they can do with it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I have both the GMC and Demon, and have now seen the example characters. It'd still be nice to see some examples of how a spirit or ghost might actually use these influances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":". 10-02-2014, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:46:40-07:00","id":270988,"title":"","content":"Page 222 of GMC describes influence and how it's used. Unfortunately, I think that's as good as an explanation as you're going to find. Werewolf's Predators book or Lore of the Forsaken might (Might) go into a bit more detail, but I don't recall that being the case. There aren't &quot;examples of play&quot; which show influences being used, or a &quot;spell list&quot; for each dot. It's a trait designed for NPCs - kind of vague so it can be flexible, and kind of powerful. The chart/section in GMC should give you enough to work with though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T15:38:32-07:00","id":271140,"title":"","content":"Yea Influences are the sort of thing that is somewhat defined by the needs of the story. It's flexible because it can do a number of things...there are not really specific systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}